      "title": "What Next?",
      "section_path": [
        "What Next?"
      ],
      "section_path_text": "What Next?",
      "level": 1,
      "ordinal": 12,
      "summary": "Rates have come up quickly and decisively since reaching their 18- month lows in January on the back of stronger vessel demand on both sides of the Suez and a tighter tonnage supply picture. Rates seem to have paused their ascent though but will probably stay strong in the near term as long as the tonnage supply picture remains tight and crude oil liftings from the Arabian Gulf and West Africa keep on growing.",
